  "home.welcomeBack": "Welcome back. Your profile is visible again.",
  "legal.privacy.summary": "DRAFT: Kuutti stores your year and month of birth, a keyed hash of your personal identity code, your self-declared gender, whom you seek, your age window, your area, your profile and photos, and a log of the photos you fetch. It never stores your personal identity code, your legal sex, your name from the bank or your date of birth. You can download everything and delete your account at any time; deletion removes your profile, photos and preferences and keeps only what the law requires.",
  "legal.privacy.title": "Privacy",
  "legal.research.summary": "DRAFT: If you say yes, anonymised events about how you use Kuutti (for example that a round was shown or a like was sent; never message text, never who you are) are kept under a separate research identifier for up to 90 days and used by the association's research partner to study how the matching works. You can withdraw at any time; withdrawing removes the link between you and the events.",
  "legal.research.title": "Research",
  "legal.special_category.summary": "DRAFT: Whom you seek, the parties you could vote for and your religion are special categories of personal data. If you say yes, Kuutti stores the answers you give to these questions: whom you seek only to match you, never shown to anyone; the parties and the religion on your card, when you choose to fill them in. None of them ever goes into a log or a research event, and you can withdraw this consent at any time, which removes the answers. Without your yes these questions stay unanswered.",
  "legal.special_category.title": "Sensitive answers",
  "legal.terms.summary": "DRAFT: Kuutti is a free dating service run by a registered association for adults living in Finland. Every account is verified with a Finnish bank login. You agree to treat other members with respect, to upload only photos of yourself, and not to copy or collect other members' photos or profiles. Kuutti may remove content and close accounts that break these terms.",
  "legal.terms.title": "Terms of use",
